## Model Tier Assignment (ENFORCED via agent frontmatter `model:` field)

Each agent pins its model in its YAML frontmatter (`~/.cursor/agents/<name>.md`). Cursor reads this field and routes the agent to the pinned model ([docs](https://cursor.com/docs/subagents#model-configuration)).

| Tier | Sub-group | Pinned Cursor model | Agents |
|------|-----------|---------------------|--------|
| **Tier A** | Deep Reasoning (opus) | `claude-4-7-opus` | Vidura, Vishwakarma, Krishna, Decision Engine, Kesh |
| **Tier A** | Deep Reasoning (sonnet) | `claude-4-6-sonnet` | Sanjaya, Vyasa, Sarthi, Money Lens, Kripacharya |
| **Tier B** | Execution / fast code | `composer-2` | Parth, Swachalit, Sutradhar, NITI |
| **Tier C** | Independent Critic | `claude-4-6-sonnet` | Bhishma, Lakshman, Draupadi |

### CRITICAL RULES — ENFORCED (STRICT)

> **Model assignment is STRICT. Each agent MUST use ONLY its assigned model.**
>
> - ❌ Do **NOT** override assigned models
> - ❌ Do **NOT** inherit models automatically (no `inherit`, no `auto` fallback in spec)
> - ❌ Do **NOT** dynamically reassign models at runtime
> - ✅ Each agent uses ONLY the model pinned in its `~/.cursor/agents/<name>.md` frontmatter

> **Executor (Parth) and Reviewer (Bhishma) MUST NEVER use the same model.**
> Current pinning: Parth = `composer-2`, Bhishma = `claude-4-6-sonnet` → invariant satisfied.
> Independent critique requires an independent model. This rule is **absolute**.

### Fallback Behavior (Cursor platform reality)

Cursor may fall back to the parent/default model if:
- The pinned model requires **Max Mode** and Max Mode is off
- The **team admin** has blocked the model
- The model is not available on the user's current **plan**

When fallback happens, it will show up in the Cursor usage report (different model than pinned). This is observable — not silent. If you see mismatches, either enable Max Mode, change plan, or swap the `model:` field in the affected agent file to a plan-compatible slug.

### Verifying model IDs

Cursor's published model catalog changes periodically. Authoritative sources:
- Cursor model picker in the IDE (your account's live list)
- [Cursor models & pricing page](https://cursor.com/docs/models-and-pricing)

If a slug in this spec (`composer-2`, `claude-4-6-sonnet`) becomes deprecated or renamed, update the `model:` field in each affected `~/.cursor/agents/<name>.md` file.

