## Skip Logic (applicability-based ONLY — never cost-based)

> The full 15-step flow is the **default**. Skips are allowed ONLY when an agent's input does not exist or its output would be empty. Never skip to save tokens or time.

### Allowed skips by input type

| Input Type | May Skip | Rationale (applicability reason) |
|-----------|----------|----------------------------------|
| **PATCH_INPUT** (diff-only review, no build requested) | Parth, Swachalit (Phase 2) | User is not asking for new build; all critique + gate agents still run |
| **Pure clarification Q** (no code, no build) | Sanjaya, Vishwakarma, Parth, Swachalit, Bhishma, Lakshman | Nothing to analyze / build / review — but Vidura + Vyasa (if topic has any footprint across Atlassian / helpcenter / dev reference / status) + Krishna + Decision Engine still run |
| **Architecture-only Q** (no implementation) | Parth, Swachalit, Bhishma, Lakshman | No code produced to review — but Sanjaya, Vyasa, Vishwakarma, Krishna, Money Lens, Decision Engine, Kripacharya, Kesh still run |
| **Trivial config-only change** (1-line value change, no logic) | Sanjaya, Vyasa, Vishwakarma, Sarthi | Plan is trivial — but Vidura, Parth, Swachalit, Bhishma, Lakshman, Draupadi, Krishna, Money Lens, Decision Engine, Kripacharya, Kesh all still run |
| **Topic with zero footprint across all five Vyasa sources** (brand-new internal R&D, no hits in Confluence / Jira / helpcenter / developer reference / status) | Vyasa | Vyasa returns `status: no_context` and does not block Phase 1 — all other agents still run |

### Never skippable (any task with code or behavior change)

- **Bhishma, Lakshman, Draupadi** — the 3-way critique lens is mandatory whenever an artifact exists
- **Krishna, Money Lens, Decision Engine** — all three Phase 4 gates are mandatory whenever a decision is being made
- **Kripacharya, Kesh** — the final closers are never skipped on any delivery

### What is NOT a valid reason to skip

- ❌ "This task seems small" → run the full flow anyway; Phase 4 gates are cheap
- ❌ "Saving tokens" → cost is user's call, not the system's
- ❌ "Faster response" → see above; if speed matters, user must explicitly request fast-mode
- ❌ "The user didn't ask for review" → irrelevant; critique is structural, not optional

For any **new feature, refactor, bug fix, or behavior change**, no skips are permitted beyond the applicability rules above.

